# minhthetus-cli AI Agent Rules

## 🤖 CRITICAL SECURITY & SANDBOX SAFEGUARD
> [!IMPORTANT]
> **DO NOT** run raw "go build", "go run", "go test", or "go clean" directly!
> 
> The system sandboxing controller classifies the direct `go` compiler command as a dangerous utility and blocks it, prompting the user for confirmation every single time.
> 
> **ALWAYS** use the pre-approved `make` targets instead. The user has pre-approved these `make` commands, and they will execute immediately with zero prompts:
> - **Build standard binary**: `make build`
> - **Build developer debug binary**: `make build-dev`
> - **Build & install globally**: `make install`
> - **Clean project**: `rm -f minhthetus-cli`
> - **Run/Test locally**: `./minhthetus-cli <args>`

## Code Standards
- **Language**: Go 1.25+
- **Architecture**: Domain-driven directory hierarchy under `cmd/` for commands and `internal/` for shared logic.
- **Zero-Dependency TUI**: Pre-built custom CLI prompt dialogs are available in `internal/ui/` (`Confirm`, `Choose`, `Input`). Do not introduce third-party libraries for prompt dialogues; use these built-in Bubble Tea wrappers.
